<title>GERMANY: Waigel - euro has chance to become anchor currency.</title>
<headline>Waigel - euro has chance to become anchor currency.</headline>
<dateline>KIEL, Germany 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel on Monday said the future European single currency, the euro, had a chance to become an &quot;anchor currency&quot; like the mark or the dollar.</p>
<p>Defending plans for monetary union, Waigel told journalists the euro would help build a strong European economy and Germany had not been well served by swings in the mark's value in the past.</p>
<p>Waigel also said Germany planned to adhere to the criteria stipulated by the Maastricht Treaty for joining monetary union and that talk of watering down the conditions would hurt acceptance of the euro.</p>
<p>--Bonn Newsroom +49 2228 16097150</p>
